أفهم الصراحة يعني منطقك عشان أنا مش فاهم. دلوقتي دلوقتي أنا في الموقع unstructured.io الملفات اترفت، يعني الملفات اترفت هناك. هل لما يحصل request جديد، أنا دلوقتي مسحت الهيستوري وهارفع ملفات، فهل لما أبعت request فهو كده هيقرأ هيخليني أحمل الملفات على طول ولا هيبدأ يعمل الفايلات من أول وجديد؟ يعني أنا أتمنى إن هو إن أنا طالما الملفات موجودة فأن\n<truncated 1667 bytes>\n4. هو ده البرنامج شغال تمام؟ ده لسه بقول بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم الاقي فيه مشاكل. أنت متأكد أن كل حاجة شغالة؟ أنت جربت عملت testing على البرنامج كله؟ عشان تقريبا يعني أنا اللي أنا شايفه ده أنت معملتش بربع جنيه test. \n5. أنت شلت الـ log بتاع الـ server وما حطيتش log بتاع الـ pipeline. قلت لك الـ pop up reading file and extract. طلعت مشكلة تانية هبعتها لك برضه. قلت لك الـ pop up يطلع على الجزء الشمال، لكن العمليات المطابقة الجديدة وسجل العمليات وإعدادات النظام تكون ظاهرين ممكن أستخدمهم في أي وقت. \n\n\r\n============================================================\r\n[*] Processing Shortages files (1 file(s))\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n  -> File: 0913.xlsx (Type: .xlsx)\r\n  -> Reading Excel file: 0913.xlsx\r\n  -> Active sheet: ورقة2\r\n  -> Header row: 6 -> ['أسم العميل', 'أسم الصنف', 'التاريخ', 'الكمية']\r\n  -> Extracted 993 data rows\r\n  -> Auto-detected drug name column: أسم الصنف\r\n  -> Extracted 993 items from column 'أسم الصنف'\r\n     Extracted items: 993\r\n\r\n=================\n<truncated 5906 bytes>\n6. looggggs فين بتاع السسرفر والpipeline\n7. معنى إن الـ loading يظهر في الجزء الشمال، فهو مش يظهر هنا. أولاً، الـ log يظهر تحت الإعدادات، لما أضغط عليه يظهر لي مربع في النص التاني فيه الحاجات اللي بتحصل في الـ terminal. أما في الإعدادات ذات نفسها، في log بتاع الـ server أنت كنت عامله قبل كده وحذفته، راح فين؟ وأنا لما أقول لك الـ loading يبقى الـ pop up على النص الشمال في الحتة اللي أنا عامل لك فيها screenshot. لكن الجزء اليمين اللي هو فيه الإعدادات والجديدة والسجل، ده أقدر أتنقل بينهم براحتي عادي، ولما أجي أتنقل، مثلاً رحت السجل وأرجع مثلاً للجديدة، فالجديدة ديت لسه شغال فيها الـ process اللي أنا لسه مشغلها. في الـ process بتاع الـ shortage\n<truncated 1531 bytes>\n8. هو انت بتعمل اي ؟\n9. هو انت مستخدم Gemini ليه؟ ما احنا عاملين سيرفر MSE، واللوج بتاع السيرفر الـ MSE مش موجود في الإعدادات ليه؟ انت كنت حاطه في الإعدادات وشلته. احنا دلوقتي بنستخدم السيرفر اللي هو الـ endpoint بتاع الـ MSE. انت ليه بتستخدم Gemini؟ \n\n============================================================\r\n[*] Processing Warehouse files (6 file(s))\r\n============================================================\r\n\r\n  -> File: السلام شبين.pdf (Type: .pdf)\r\n📄 تم العثور على الملف في الذاكرة المؤقتة (Cache). جاري تحميل البيانات المستخرجة مباشرة: السلام شبين.pdf\r\n     -> Basic extraction yielded 0 items. Attempting Gemini AI extraction...\r\nDirect use of automatic function calling (AFC) in Models.generate_content is not recommended. Instead, we recommend to use AFC in Chat.send_message. Similar\n<truncated 1449 bytes>\n10. كمل\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# Continuation Summary — Pharmacy Matcher Desktop App\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n### Clarify Gemini Usage vs. MSE Server (Status: IMPLEMENTATION)\n- **User's intent**: \"هو انت مستخدم Gemini ليه؟ ما احنا عاملين سيرفر MSE... انت ليه بتستخدم Gemini؟\"\n- **Current State**: The user is confused because they saw Gemini logs and thought it was replacing their local MSE server. The local MSE server is used strictly for *matching* (fuzzy matching). Gemini is used strictly as a *fallback for extracting tables from messy PDFs* when the Unstructured API fails (returns 0 items).\n- **Next Step**: Draft a clear response explaining this architectural separation so the user understands Gemini is just an extraction assistant, not the matcher.\n\n### Fix/Clarify MSE Server Logs in Settings (Status: DISCOVERY / IMPLEMENTATION)\n- **User's intent**: \"واللوج بتاع السيرفر الـ MSE مش موجود في الإعدادات ليه؟ انت كنت حاطه في الإعدادات وشلته.\"\n- **Current State**: The HTML element `<textarea id=\"system-logs\">` *is* still in the `screen-settings` div (line 1073). However, the user believes it was removed. This might be a CSS visibility issue, a JS error preventing it from updating, or confusion between this textarea and the newly added \"Terminal\" (`screen-logs`) sidebar tab.\n- **Next Step**: Check `index.html` (specifically JS functions like `updateServerStatus` and `loadLogs`) to ensure MSE server logs are still properly routed to `#system-logs` and that it is visible to the user.\n\n### Multi-language UI Support (Status: SUGGESTED)\n- **User's intent**: \"عايز ممكن نضيف لغة ثانية اللي هو الإنجليزي في البرنامج... وتظبط حوار الـ right to left وleft to right\"\n- **Remaining Work**: Postponed until core extraction, logging, and UI stability are confirmed.\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n\n### Direct User Quotes & Feedback\n- **On Gemini Usage**: \"هو انت مستخدم Gemini ليه؟ ما احنا عاملين سيرفر MSE، واللوج بتاع السيرفر الـ MSE مش موجود في الإعدادات ليه؟ انت كنت حاطه في الإعدادات وشلته. احنا دلوقتي بنستخدم السيرفر اللي هو الـ endpoint بتاع الـ MSE. انت ليه بتستخدم Gemini؟\"\n- **On Gemini Model Error**: User shared terminal output showing `gemini-2.5-flash` returning a 404: `This model models/gemini-2.5-flash is no longer available to new users. Please update your code to use models/gemini-3.6-flash...`\n- **On UI Layout (Progress Widget)**: \"ولما أقول لك الـ loading يبقى الـ pop up على النص الشمال في الحتة اللي أنا عامل لك فيها screenshot... أقدر أتنقل بينهم براحتي عادي.\"\n- **On File Formats**: \"أنت كنت مفكر الملفات متوحدة، أنا قلت لك الملفات تختلف، التنسيقات تختلف... ما تبقاش حاطط fixed code، كل حاجه بتتغير.\"\n\n### Context Provided\n- **API Keys**: User has an Unstructured API key and a Gemini API key stored in their `.env` file, loaded via `src/config.py`.\n- **MSEMAX API Key**: `[REDACTED_CREDENTIAL]` (Server at `D:\\AI_Engineer\\MSEMAX\\`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n\n- **Fixed UI Scrolling / Responsiveness**: Added CSS media queries (`@media (max-width: 1100px)` and `@media (max-width: 768px)`) to `index.html` to make `.upload-grid`, `.settings-grid`, `.stats-grid`, and `.workflow-steps` wrap responsively. This fixes the user's complaint about rigid scrolling behavior on smaller screens.\n- **Updated Gemini Model Configuration**: Changed `gemini_model` from `gemini-3.5-flash` (or 2.5) to `gemini-3.6-flash` in `src/config.py` in direct response to the user's provided 404 API error log.\n- **Verified Progress Modal Positioning**: Confirmed that `#progress-modal` is correctly placed inside `#screen-new` with `position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0;`. Because its parent (`.main-content`) is `position: relative`, the modal safely covers *only* the left pane, allowing the user to click the right-hand sidebar freely during processing.\n- **Gemini Fallback Integration (Prior Checkpoint)**: Wired `gemini_api_key` through `backend.py` -> `read_input_files` -> `_process_pdf_file` & `_process_json_file` so Gemini acts as a robust fallback when Unstructured fails to parse messy PDFs.\n- **Dedicated Terminal Logs UI (Prior Checkpoint)**: Created `#screen-logs` (سجل النظام Terminal) to hold the pipeline logs in a dedicated view, removing it from the progress popup.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n\n### Architecture & Workflows\n- **Logging Architecture**: There are two distinct log view elements in `index.html`:\n  1. `#system-logs` (Textarea inside the Settings screen)\n  2. `#pipeline-log-terminal` (Textarea inside the new Terminal screen)\n  Both listen to `window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('new_log', ...))` triggered by `backend.py` via `self.window.evaluate_js()`. The user's claim that the MSE server log was \"removed from settings\" requires investigating if JS is failing to append to `#system-logs` or if the user is simply misunderstanding the new Terminal tab split.\n- **Separation of Concerns (Gemini vs. MSE)**: \n  - *Gemini*: Exclusively used in `src/extract/file_handler.py` as a fallback parser. It takes raw text/JSON from the Unstructured API and extracts tabular rows using LLM reasoning.\n  - *MSE Server*: Exclusively used for fuzzy matching extracted shortage names against the warehouse lists. \n- **Pywebview Quirks**: The app uses `pywebview` for the desktop wrapper. Any UI thread updates or native dialogs must be handled carefully (deprecation warnings for `OPEN_DIALOG` were fixed by attempting `FileDialog.OPEN` first).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html`**\n  - *What*: Added responsive `@media` queries around line 660 for `.upload-grid`, `.settings-grid`, etc. Verified positioning of `#progress-modal` and `#system-logs`.\n  - *Why*: To fix the rigid scrolling layout on smaller screens.\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\src\\config.py`**\n  - *What*: Changed `gemini_model` string to `\"gemini-3.6-flash\"`.\n  - *Why*: To fix the `404 NOT_FOUND` error reported by the user for deprecated models.\n\n### Viewed Files (Key Context)\n- **`d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\backend.py`**\n  - *File Landscape*: Contains the PyWebview API class (`AppApi`) bridging the frontend JS to the backend Python logic.\n  - *Key Sections*: Investigated around `self.window.evaluate_js`. Confirmed `new_log` events are being fired from the backend to populate the frontend terminal/log textareas.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n**Current Status:** Execution was interrupted by a system restart just as we were about to explain the Gemini usage to the user and investigate the missing MSE logs in settings.\n\n**Immediate Next Steps:**\n1. **Draft User Response**: Explain to the user *exactly* why Gemini is being used (it is ONLY a fallback for reading messy PDFs when the Unstructured API fails, whereas the MSE server is used exclusively for matching the items later). \n2. **Investigate MSE Logs in Settings**: Open `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy\\desktop_app\\templates\\index.html` and inspect the JS around `updateServerStatus` or the `new_log` event listener (around line 1120). Verify why the user believes the MSE server log \"was removed\" from the settings page, even though `<textarea id=\"system-logs\">` is still present in the HTML. Fix the routing or visibility if it is broken.\n3. **Notify User of Fixes**: Inform the user that the Gemini model has been updated to `gemini-3.6-flash` to fix the 404 error they encountered.\n\nYou have the 23 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/desktop-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:17:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/pharmacy-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T10:46:04Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006220414]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006220414.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006245677]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006245677.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790008142552]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790008142552.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T16:29:03Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790030764891]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790030764891.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:46:21Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790030964763]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790030964763.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:49:25Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790031115353]\nPath