{"step_index":1220,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T01:24:59Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T04:24:59+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T04:25:02+03:00\nThe search for \"\"https://transform.unstructured.io\" extract schema parse_id\" returned the following summary:\nTo extract data using Unstructured's API with a defined schema, you typically utilize the `structured_data_extractor` within a workflow job[1][2].\n\n### How to Use Extraction with Schema\nThe `parse_id` is generally associated with the result of a partitioning or processing job[3]. When using the API for structured extraction, you define your requirements in a JSON schema and include them in the `job_nodes` configuration of your request[2].\n\n#### Example API Request Structure\nYou can perform extraction by sending a `POST` request to the Unstructured API. Below is the conceptual structure for a job that performs both parsing and structured extraction[2]:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"job_nodes\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Partitioner\",\n      \"type\": \"partition\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vlm\",\n      \"settings\": { \"is_dynamic\": true, \"allow_fast\": true }\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Extractor\",\n      \"type\": \"structured_data_extractor\",\n      \"subtype\": \"llm\",\n      \"settings\": {\n        \"schema_to_extract\": {\n          \"json_schema\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"field_name\": { \"type\": \"string\" }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\"field_name\"]\n          },\n          \"extraction_guidance\": \"Instructions for the model...\"\n        },\n        \"provider\": \"openai\",\n        \"model\": \"gpt-5-mini\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Key Steps\n1.  **Define Your Schema**: Your schema must conform to **OpenAI’s Structured Outputs guidelines**[1]. Note that there is a maximum nesting depth of 10 levels for JSON schemas[1].\n2.  **API Integration**: Use the `/jobs/` endpoint to submit your document and your `job_nodes` configuration (as shown above)[2].\n3.  **Extraction Methods**: In the Unstructured UI or API, you can choose between **LLM** (default) or **Regex** methods for extraction[1].\n4.  **Workflow**: If you are using the Unstructured web interface, you can define your schema visually in the **Define Schema** pane after uploading a file[1][4]. The \"Get Code\" feature in the UI can also generate the specific API request code for your defined workflow[3][5].\n\nFor detailed implementation, refer to the [Unstructured API reference documentation](https://docs.unstructured.io/api-reference/workflow/workflows)[6].\n\nSources:\n[1] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEIhfXAfBFnJ98UwDKYMS_a6Mx77jhVrOmEBx8yT1IdlPyAvV_GvCZ_rF8Ww7xH3Gv7xELjWBJ3KKowS3JkNp40u9iFuz40L3o-gy0auA18Ueafk6ZfcAgH2lILAfP77QEGaO7z4Qj6eKe5c8QnBtZ3_mY3ftPKW8HLSvd2JNd-TS2KzWZZedO7J4vuZQYmgc87Pl-c_75AhAY=)\n[2] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHZBH1dkJg_1jdudeW46f4syTpkWldsoc95SMz9gTaOwIOONxo0MXb7N0O_X1Pqcw8coqo3fJwVYYRpGZJbAecI7Y4YjCd4D9dJtvEjI5V3tHKhX_dzRyWynpdPC5fbiFG7QEuLaLIK6i8Q1NEIubOBmzc1A6j2pmIo4N3xuA==)\n[3] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH6thzFMCwznq1PAWL7fqE3RuTKopatHoSkRsP0MhY34xgKBETj-n6uGh5SAXD8-QmdTzjKEInM4ariziCS0tU4ON4PpDFWlponBYVCAwkMvUi3DEswEPNWrr1tzUAIaxHCJfR6496e4FiQ)\n[4] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEIhfXAfBFnJ98UwDKYMS_a6Mx77jhVrOmEBx8yT1IdlPyAvV_GvCZ_rF8Ww7xH3Gv7xELjWBJ3KKowS3JkNp40u9iFuz40L3o-gy0auA18Ueafk6ZfcAgH2lILAfP77QEGaO7z4Qj6eKe5c8QnBtZ3_mY3ftPKW8HLSvd2JNd-TS2KzWZZedO7J4vuZQYmgc87Pl-c_75AhAY=)\n[5] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH6thzFMCwznq1PAWL7fqE3RuTKopatHoSkRsP0MhY34xgKBETj-n6uGh5SAXD8-QmdTzjKEInM4ariziCS0tU4ON4PpDFWlponBYVCAwkMvUi3DEswEPNWrr1t